    <section class="chapter" id="ch8">
        <h2 class="chapter-title">Chapter 8 — The Evaluation Harness</h2>

        <div class="concept">
            <h3>Why LLM-as-Judge?</h3>
            <p>You can't write <code>assert(output === expected)</code> for LLMs — there's no single correct answer. LLM-as-judge: a second LLM reads the response and scores it on specific dimensions.</p>
        </div>

        <div class="concept">
            <h3>The Four Scoring Dimensions (0-3 each, 12 max, pass = 8)</h3>
            <table class="info-table">
                <tr><th>Dimension</th><th>Catches</th><th>Score 0</th><th>Score 3</th></tr>
                <tr><td><strong>Groundedness</strong></td><td>Hallucination</td><td>Wrong pricing</td><td>Cites correct KB facts</td></tr>
                <tr><td><strong>Relevance</strong></td><td>Wrong answer</td><td>Talks about CDN when asked about Workers</td><td>Directly addresses the question</td></tr>
                <tr><td><strong>Role-appropriateness</strong></td><td>System prompt failure</td><td>CLI tutorial for an AE</td><td>Business framing for AE</td></tr>
                <tr><td><strong>Actionability</strong></td><td>Unusable output</td><td>Academic essay</td><td>Usable in a sales call TODAY</td></tr>
            </table>
        </div>

        <div class="callout">
            <h3>Score Progression</h3>
            <p><strong>67%</strong> → Groundedness failures. Added "CRITICAL RULE: use specific facts from KB."</p>
            <p><strong>73%</strong> → Role-appropriateness failures. Added DEPTH RULES per role.</p>
            <p><strong>87%</strong> → Two remaining edge cases documented. Acceptable for v1.</p>
        </div>

        <div class="callout" style="border-color: #ef4444;">
            <h3>Self-Grading Bias (Known Weakness)</h3>
            <p>Agent uses Llama 3.3 70B. Judge also uses Llama 3.3 70B. The judge is biased toward responses matching its own style → inflated scores. Fix: use Claude as judge via Anthropic API.</p>
        </div>

        <div class="questions">
            <h3>Interview Questions</h3>
            <details><summary>Q: How do you evaluate AI quality?</summary>
            <div><p>LLM-as-judge. Python harness runs 15 test cases against the live API, then a second LLM scores each on 4 dimensions (0-3): groundedness, relevance, role-appropriateness, actionability. Pass: 8/12. Run after every prompt change. Progression: 67% → 73% → 87%.</p></div></details>
            <details><summary>Q: What is self-grading bias?</summary>
            <div><p>Using the same model as agent and judge. The judge is lenient toward responses matching its own style. Fix: different model as judge (Claude via Anthropic API).</p></div></details>
            <details><summary>Q: How did you improve from 67% to 87%?</summary>
            <div><p>Iteration-driven prompt engineering. At 67%: groundedness failures → added CRITICAL RULE requiring specific KB facts. At 73%: role-appropriateness failures → added role-specific DEPTH RULES. At 87%: two documented edge cases remaining.</p></div></details>
        </div>
    </section>

