    <section class="chapter" id="ch11">
        <h2 class="chapter-title">Chapter 11 — The Behavioral Story</h2>

        <div class="callout">
            <h3>The 60-Second Pitch</h3>
            <p><em>"I built a multi-agent intelligence platform for sales teams on Cloudflare's edge network. Three AI agents — account research, sales coaching, and transcript analysis — each running as a Durable Object with per-user conversation history and role-based access control. The system uses RAG with a curated knowledge base, streaming SSE for real-time token delivery, and a two-tier memory system that extracts personal facts from conversations and remembers them across sessions. I built an eval harness with LLM-as-judge scoring that improved pass rates from 67% to 87% across three prompt engineering iterations. Deployed live on Cloudflare Workers at zero infrastructure cost."</em></p>
        </div>

        <div class="concept">
            <h3>The 5-Minute Deep Dive</h3>
            <p><strong>Minute 1 — The problem:</strong> Sales reps waste 30-60 min per call doing manual research. They miss things. AI answers hallucinate.</p>
            <p><strong>Minute 2 — The architecture:</strong> Three agents, each a Durable Object. Hono router with JWT auth + rate limiting. DO SQLite for history. Tools run before the LLM. SSE streaming.</p>
            <p><strong>Minute 3 — The hard problem:</strong> Two-tier memory. Short-term in DO SQLite (serial access). Long-term in KV (cross-agent sharing). The <code>waitUntil()</code> bug where extraction was silently failing.</p>
            <p><strong>Minute 4 — The eval story:</strong> Python eval harness. LLM-as-judge. 4 dimensions. 67% → 73% → 87%. Self-grading bias acknowledged.</p>
            <p><strong>Minute 5 — What I'd change:</strong> Reranking. Claude as judge. Summarize old turns. More aggressive LTM extraction.</p>
        </div>

        <div class="concept">
            <h3>Anthropic Screening Questions → Your Answers</h3>
            <p><strong>"Have you built and deployed a production LLM-powered application?"</strong><br/>
            → Yes. <code>se-intel-portfolio.stephenmack96.workers.dev</code>. 3 agents, real auth, rate limiting, audit trails. Not a demo.</p>

            <p><strong>"Have you built AI agents with tool use capabilities?"</strong><br/>
            → Yes. AccountIntelAgent dispatches 3 tools (news, KB search, web search) based on intent. RBAC enforced at tool execution time. Audit logged.</p>

            <p><strong>"Describe experience with LLMs creating complex functionality."</strong><br/>
            → Multi-agent system with streaming, cross-session memory (LLM extraction → KV), role-calibrated prompts, and an eval harness with score progression.</p>

            <p><strong>"Do you have expertise coding in Python?"</strong><br/>
            → Yes. Eval harness: runner.py, judge.py, report.py. httpx, dotenv, argparse. Calls Workers AI REST API directly.</p>
